CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'num == 0'
#300: FILE: drivers/irqchip/irq-gic-v2m.c:207:
+	if ((num == 0) || (base + num > V2M_MAX_SPI)) {

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*v2m)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct v2m_data)...)
#315: FILE: drivers/irqchip/irq-gic-v2m.c:222:
+	v2m = kzalloc(sizeof(struct v2m_data), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

